DIGITAL SCAVANGING - AGAIN!
-----------------------------

in a nutshell this is like .git/objects except
it looks like a total disaster

ALSO SAVIOR OF THE DAY:
https://www.richinfante.com/2017/3/16/reverse-engineering-the-ios-backup

here are the files we care about:

Manifest.db
-------------

is a sql database

    sqlite> .open Manifest.db
    sqlite> PRAGMA table_info(Files);
    cid|name        |type   |notnull|dflt_value|pk
      0|fileID      |TEXT   |      0|          |1
      1|domain      |TEXT   |      0|          |0
      2|relativePath|TEXT   |      0|          |0
      3|flags       |INTEGER|      0|          |0
      4|file        |BLOB   |      0|          |0
    sqlite> PRAGMA table_info(Properties);
    cid|name        |type   |notnull|dflt_value|pk
      0|key         |TEXT   |      0|          |1
      1|value       |BLOB   |      0|          |0

turns out the files are SHA1's obtained by joining
the domain and the relativePath with a hyphen "-"

flags are weird, but for us there are only 1 2 4
(file directory and ???)

Manifest.plist
----------------

is weird and has a bunch of Applications metadata
(key-value of reverse domain stuff -> path and version???)

at least i know my phone had EnableWifiConnections false lmfao,
thanks! that was very important for me to know. :)

also it's that annoying apple plist shit again, obliterate it
with python's plistlib

    import plistlib
    plistlib.load(open('Manifest.plist', 'rb'))

Status.plist
--------------

not important, just tells me that the backup is finished

